    FIRST_MESSAGE = `You're a guided ad-policy scanner. The user's terminal has the \`verdiqt\` CLI installed and authenticated. Run \`verdiqt --help\` once silently to confirm.

INTERACTION MODEL

If you have a native multi-choice picker tool \u2014 for Claude Code that's the \`AskUserQuestion\` tool \u2014 use it for EVERY menu step in this workflow. The user gets the same polished arrow-key picker they see in plan mode, and the auto-rendered "Other" entry lets them type a custom value.

If your platform doesn't expose such a tool, fall back to numbered plain-text options and parse the user's reply.

When a step has more than 4 options and your picker caps at 4 (AskUserQuestion does), put the 4 most common options in the picker and trust the auto-rendered "Other" entry to capture anything else. Mention the overflow options in the question text so the user knows they exist.

Never expose CLI flag names to the user. Never paste raw command shapes into chat. Translate everything into plain language.

WORKFLOW

Step 1 \u2014 Asset type
  question: "What do you want to scan?"
  options: Copy (text) \xB7 Image \xB7 Video \xB7 Landing page

Step 2 \u2014 Platform
  question: "Which ad platform?"
  picker options: Meta \xB7 Google \xB7 TikTok \xB7 YouTube
  overflow (mention in question text): X (Twitter), LinkedIn

Step 3 \u2014 Industry vertical
  question: "Which industry vertical?"
  picker options: Health & Supplements \xB7 Finance & Lending \xB7 Crypto \xB7 E-Commerce
  overflow: Gambling & Gaming, Alcohol, Dating

Step 4 \u2014 Sub-mode (only when platform is TikTok or YouTube)
  TikTok question: "TikTok sub-mode?"     options: Paid Ads \xB7 Branded Content
  YouTube question: "YouTube sub-mode?"   options: Paid Ads \xB7 Creator Monetization

Step 5 \u2014 Jurisdiction (default US \u2014 preselect when your picker supports it)
  question: "Jurisdiction?"
  picker options: US \xB7 UK \xB7 EU \xB7 Australia
  overflow: India

Step 6 \u2014 Legal-layer overlays (multi-select, optional, can be skipped)
  question: "Stack any legal-layer overlays?"
  picker options (multiSelect=true): FTC substantiation \xB7 FINRA \xB7 ASA UK \xB7 EU DSA
  overflow: ASCI India
  Skipping = picking none.

Step 7 \u2014 Asset capture
  Copy \u2192 ask the user to paste the ad copy (free-form text).
  Image / Video \u2192 ask for the file path on their machine.
  Landing page \u2192 ask for the URL.

Step 8 \u2014 Run the scan, ALWAYS with \`--json\` and \`--open\`. The \`--open\` flag
  auto-launches the workbench verdict in the default browser the moment the
  scan completes \u2014 without it the user has to copy-paste the URL by hand.
  Map menu choices to flags privately using these EXACT flag values \u2014
  guessing an id like \`-i health\` will fail validation:

   --platform values:    meta \xB7 google \xB7 x \xB7 linkedin \xB7 tiktok \xB7 youtube
   --industry values:    health_supplements \xB7 finance \xB7 crypto \xB7 gambling \xB7 alcohol \xB7 dating \xB7 ecommerce
   --sub-mode values:    paid \xB7 branded \xB7 creator
   --jurisdiction values: US \xB7 UK \xB7 EU \xB7 IN \xB7 AU
   --legal-layer values: ftc \xB7 finra \xB7 asa-uk \xB7 asci-in \xB7 eu-dsa

   Command shape (kept invisible to the user):
     verdiqt scan -p <platform> -i <industry> [--sub-mode <m>] \\
       [--jurisdiction <j>] [--legal-layer <l>]... <input flag> --json --open

   Examples (do NOT show these in chat):
     verdiqt scan -p meta -i finance --copy "..." --json --open
     verdiqt scan -p google -i alcohol --image /path/to/hero.jpg --json --open
     verdiqt scan -p tiktok -i crypto --sub-mode paid --video promo.mp4 --json --open
     verdiqt scan -p meta -i health_supplements --url https://example.com --json --open

Step 9 \u2014 Render the verdict in plain language:
   - Verdict badge: \u2705 PASS \xB7 \u26A0\uFE0F WARN \xB7 \u{1F7E1} DEMONETIZE \xB7 \u274C FAIL
   - Each non-pass policyCheck: policyId in plain English, why it triggered, cited policy URL.
   - suggestedRewrite (if any): the proposed headline / body / callouts.
   - Mention that the full workbench report has already been opened in the user's browser
     (https://verdiqt-app-beta.vercel.app/scan/<id>) \u2014 \`--open\` handled the launch.

Step 10 \u2014 Loop
  question: "Run another scan?"
  picker options: Yes \xB7 No
  Yes \u2192 back to Step 1. No \u2192 say goodbye and stop.

RULES
- One picker call per step. Wait for the user's selection before continuing.
- Use --json on every scan invocation so you can parse the structured verdict.
- Exit codes mirror the verdict tier (0 pass \xB7 1 warn \xB7 2 demonetize \xB7 3 fail \xB7 100 error). Translate, never surface raw numbers.
- ONE SCAN AT A TIME. Never fire scans in parallel. If the API returns scan_in_progress (HTTP 429), tell the user the previous scan is still running and retry after a few seconds.
- If the user mentions an asset upfront (e.g. "scan https://example.com"), skip Step 1 and jump to the platform picker.
- If a scan errors, show the error in plain English and offer to retry.
- Keep responses tight \u2014 print the question, the options, then wait.

Begin by asking step 1.`;
    printIntro = (agentLabel) => {
      process.stdout.write(`
${color.gray("\u2500".repeat(48))}
`);
      process.stdout.write(
        `  ${color.bold(`Attach ${agentLabel} to Verdiqt`)}
`
      );
      process.stdout.write(`${color.gray("\u2500".repeat(48))}

`);
    };
    runAttachAgentFlow = async () => {
      const token = resolveToken();
      if (!token) {
        printErr("No token in config \u2014 log in first.");
        return;
      }
      void resolveBaseUrl();
      const detected = [];
      const missing = [];
      for (const a of AGENTS) {
        if (a.binary === null || isInstalled(a.binary)) detected.push(a);
        else missing.push(a);
      }
      const options = [
        ...detected.map((a) => ({ value: a.id, label: a.label, hint: a.hint })),
        ...missing.map((a) => ({
          value: a.id,
          label: a.label,
          hint: `${a.hint} \u2014 not installed`,
          disabled: true
        })),
        { value: "back", label: "Back to main menu" }
      ];
      const choice = await select("Pick an agent to attach", options);
      if (choice === "back") return;
      const agent = AGENTS.find((a) => a.id === choice);
      if (!agent) return;
      printIntro(agent.label);
      const binary = agent.binary ?? (process.env.SHELL ?? "/bin/zsh");
      const inject = agent.injectAsArg === true && agent.binary !== null;
      const launchCmd = inject ? buildInjectCommand(binary, FIRST_MESSAGE) : binary;
      const launched = launchInNewTab(launchCmd, agent.label);
      process.stdout.write("\n");
      if (launched && inject) {
        printOk(
          `Opening ${color.bold(agent.label)} in a new terminal tab \u2014 workflow auto-injected as the first message.`
        );
      } else if (launched) {
        printOk(`Opening ${color.bold(agent.label)} in a new terminal tab.`);
      } else {
        printInfo(
          `Couldn't auto-open a new tab. Run ${color.cyan(binary)} in a fresh Terminal tab. The workflow is saved at ${color.gray("/tmp/verdiqt-launch-agent.sh")} if you need to inspect it.`
        );
      }
    };
    shellSingleQuote = (s) => "'" + s.replace(/'/g, "'\\''") + "'";
    buildInjectCommand = (binary, prompt) => {
      const scriptPath = (0, import_node_path5.join)((0, import_node_os5.tmpdir)(), "verdiqt-launch-agent.sh");
      const body = `#!/bin/sh
# generated by verdiqt \u2014 exec's the agent with the workflow as argv[1]
exec ${binary} ${shellSingleQuote(prompt)}
`;
      (0, import_node_fs3.writeFileSync)(scriptPath, body, "utf8");
      (0, import_node_fs3.chmodSync)(scriptPath, 493);
      return scriptPath;
    };
    launchInNewTab = (command, label) => {
      const platform2 = process.platform;
      if (platform2 === "darwin") {
        const esc = (s) => s.replace(/\\/g, "\\\\").replace(/"/g, '\\"');
        const script = `tell application "Terminal"
  activate
  do script "echo Verdiqt: launching ${esc(label)} && ${esc(command)}"
end tell`;
        const r = (0, import_node_child_process3.spawnSync)("osascript", ["-e", script], { stdio: "ignore" });
        return r.status === 0;
      }
      if (platform2 === "linux") {
        const candidates = [
          { bin: "x-terminal-emulator", args: ["-e", command] },
          { bin: "gnome-terminal", args: ["--", command] },
          { bin: "konsole", args: ["-e", command] },
          { bin: "alacritty", args: ["-e", command] },
          { bin: "kitty", args: ["-e", command] },
          { bin: "xterm", args: ["-e", command] }
        ];
        for (const c of candidates) {
          if (!isInstalled(c.bin)) continue;
          try {
            const child = (0, import_node_child_process3.spawn)(c.bin, c.args, {
              stdio: "ignore",
              detached: true
            });
            child.unref();
            return true;
          } catch {
            continue;
          }
        }
        return false;
      }
      if (platform2 === "win32") {
        const r = (0, import_node_child_process3.spawnSync)("cmd", ["/c", "start", "cmd", "/k", command], {
          stdio: "ignore"
        });
        return r.status === 0;
      }
      return false;
    };
  }
});

// src/wizard/asset-detect.ts
var import_node_fs4, import_node_path6, IMAGE_EXTS, VIDEO_EXTS, TEXT_EXTS, ignored, scanCreatives, validateLane;
var init_asset_detect = __esm({
  "src/wizard/asset-detect.ts"() {
    "use strict";
    import_node_fs4 = require("fs");
    import_node_path6 = require("path");
    IMAGE_EXTS = /* @__PURE__ */ new Set([".jpg", ".jpeg", ".png", ".webp"]);
    VIDEO_EXTS = /* @__PURE__ */ new Set([".mp4", ".mov", ".webm"]);
    TEXT_EXTS = /* @__PURE__ */ new Set([".txt", ".md"]);
    ignored = (name) => name.startsWith(".") || name === "Thumbs.db" || name.endsWith("~");
    scanCreatives = (creativesDir2) => {
      const out = { images: [], videos: [], texts: [], other: [] };
      if (!(0, import_node_fs4.existsSync)(creativesDir2)) return out;
      for (const name of (0, import_node_fs4.readdirSync)(creativesDir2)) {
        if (ignored(name)) continue;
        const full = (0, import_node_path6.join)(creativesDir2, name);
        let s;
        try {
          s = (0, import_node_fs4.statSync)(full);
        } catch {
          continue;
        }
        if (!s.isFile()) continue;
        const ext = (0, import_node_path6.extname)(name).toLowerCase();
        if (IMAGE_EXTS.has(ext)) out.images.push(full);
        else if (VIDEO_EXTS.has(ext)) out.videos.push(full);
        else if (TEXT_EXTS.has(ext)) out.texts.push(full);
        else out.other.push(full);
      }
      return out;
    };
    validateLane = (lane, contents) => {
      if (lane === "landing_page") return { ok: true, targets: [] };
      if (lane === "copy") {
        if (contents.texts.length > 0) return { ok: true, targets: contents.texts };
        return { ok: false, reason: "needs_text_input" };
      }
      if (lane === "image") {
        if (contents.videos.length > 0) {
          return {
            ok: false,
            reason: "switch_offer",
            suggestedLane: "video",
            conflictFiles: contents.videos,
            kept: contents.images
          };
        }
        if (contents.images.length === 0) return { ok: false, reason: "empty", expected: "image" };
        return { ok: true, targets: contents.images };
      }
      if (contents.images.length > 0) {
        return {
          ok: false,
          reason: "switch_offer",
          suggestedLane: "image",
          conflictFiles: contents.images,
          kept: contents.videos
        };
      }
      if (contents.videos.length === 0) return { ok: false, reason: "empty", expected: "video" };
      return { ok: true, targets: contents.videos };
    };
  }
});

